            "title": "HOCs and Props",
            "concept": "HOCs and Props is about passing props through a HOC, which must spread them onto the wrapped component so nothing is lost. In Higher-Order Components, this matters because the pattern decides how the interface behaves when real data arrives. Used well, it keeps the component small, predictable and easy to test, so the rest of the app can rely on it.",
            "syntax": "<WrappedComponent {...props} />",
