            "title": "HOCs vs Hooks",
            "concept": "HOCs vs Hooks is about the difference between HOCs and hooks: hooks share logic without adding components to the tree, while HOCs wrap components. In Higher-Order Components, this matters because the pattern decides how the interface behaves when real data arrives. Used well, it keeps the component small, predictable and easy to test, so the rest of the app can rely on it.",
